{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1321937-opnet-as-a-game-resource","id":1321937,"title":"OpNet as a game resource?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-02T16:08:53-07:00","id":1321937,"title":"OpNet as a game resource?","content":"I was thinking about creating a wiki of in character information for my Aeon game.<br /> Ideally it would have a central repository of cannon information (maybe using git?) that individual SGs could then clone to their own local wikis, and modify to suit their setting.<br /> so, Q&amp;A<br /> Does something like this already exist?<br /> Any recommendations on software/services to use?<br /> Ideas for loading the initial Cannon? Trying to avoid a big manual effort.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if the wiki could have on-page comments (SG provided) to emulate user comments (think like the comments in Shadowrun equipment sections)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T05:11:57-07:00","id":1327557,"title":"","content":"Dumb question, what is git?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T12:37:39-07:00","id":1327633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1321937-opnet-as-a-game-resource?p=1327557#post1327557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question, what is git?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://git-scm.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://git-scm.com/</a> - distributed version control. Its the same version control software that is associated with GitHub if you've ever heard of that. In this context I would expect it would support maintaining a common set of data that can be distributed (and updated) to multiple users without those users having to access a single, central copy. Since it would be cloned, you could also add your own local information without it necessarily getting added to the copy that everyone gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}